Subject: [PATCH] Prioritize KRA content over the generic ZIP signature

KRA's content rules identify the document's MIME marker, but have the same
priority as the generic ZIP signature. QMimeXMLProvider warns about the
unrelated equal-priority matches when examining a KRA document's contents.
Give the more specific KRA rules higher priority, retaining recognition
of both the ZIP and legacy gzip variants without changing MIME inheritance.

The upstream file retains its original copyright and license notices.

diff --git a/krita/data/mime-database/freedesktop.org.xml b/krita/data/mime-database/freedesktop.org.xml
--- a/krita/data/mime-database/freedesktop.org.xml
+++ b/krita/data/mime-database/freedesktop.org.xml
@@ -14897,7 +14897,7 @@
     <comment xml:lang="zh-CN">Krita 文档</comment>
     <comment xml:lang="zh-TW">Krita 文件</comment>
     <generic-icon name="x-office-document"/>
-    <magic priority="60">
+    <magic priority="70">
       <match type="string" value="\037\213" offset="0">
         <match type="string" value="KOffice" offset="10">
           <match type="string" value="application/x-krita\004\006" offset="18"/>
